fpview.patch - the view modes of the native build (overhead / action / chase / shoulder / first
person): the changes to files other work owns.  docs/issues/native-first-person.md says what it
is, how a view is selected, and what was run.

Made against tools/recomp as it stood at the time in the line "snapshot" below.  Apply from
tools/recomp:

    cd tools/recomp && patch -p1 --dry-run < app/fpview.patch && patch -p1 < app/fpview.patch

The new files it needs are already in place and are not in the patch (nothing compiles them
until app/build.py is patched):
    app/fpview.h  app/fpview.cpp

Notes for the merge
 - hle.txt gains 5 addresses (tasks_call, camera_updateFocus, worldtex_stream, Player_draw,
   Camera_followZoomInput).  funcs.h changes with them, so every translation is made again and
   compiled again at its next build (about 2 minutes each).  A program that does not link
   app/fpview.cpp gets the weak pass-through of hle_weak.cpp: the game as before.  They are in
   hle.txt and not in app/hle-app.txt so that rta_app_orig (the unpatched translation the rig
   is compared with) has them too.
 - app/build.py links app/fpview.cpp into both rta_app and rta_app_orig, after gfx_rt.cpp.
   app/build_win.py is NOT touched: the Windows program keeps working without the views (weak
   pass-through; rt_dma_skip stays null).  To give it the views: add app/fpview.cpp to its job
   list beside gfx_rt.cpp, call fpview::install() after gfxrt::install() in win_main.cpp, and
   take over the --view / "app view" / V-key lines of app_main.cpp.
 - rt/rt.h, rt/runtime.cpp: two new things, both inert unless fpview uses them.  rt_dma_skip (a
   null pointer otherwise): a DMA tag on channel 1 whose data is left out of the stream (the
   local player's model in first person).  rt_unit_cost(c, cycles): the price of a unit of
   translated code on the virtual clock, 4 as before unless changed; fpview sets 0 for the
   length of a draw pass built for a view of its own and 4 again after it.  now() and the
   slice accounting in reschedule() go through slice_cycles(); with the price never changed
   they compute what they computed.
 - app/gfx_rt.h, gfx_rt.cpp: two small functions for fpview (projection_args,
   set_depth_range) and one branch at the head of scaled() that is not taken unless a view
   has set a depth range.  Widescreen itself is unchanged; the views go through it (a view's
   projection is built by fn_0018619c and the three mat4_setProjection hooks like the game's).
 - app/settings.h: lines "view = ..." and "view.<mode>.<name> = ..." are kept and handed to
   fpview::setting; Settings::save takes the view lines as a second argument.
 - app/app_main.cpp: --view, --view-set, the script / control-socket command "app view ...",
   the V key (not in a test window, like F), fpview::install() after gfxrt::install().
 - Default is "overhead": with it fpview's draw-pass hook returns before reading or writing
   anything, and the four other hooks are the plain call of the original.  The rig session
   with the patched build in overhead gives merge/rig-final-compare.txt, the same file.
 - fpview chains itself in front of rt_frame_hook (it notes two times for --opt view-timing
   and hands on to gfx_rt's): fpview::install() must stay after gfxrt::install().
